+# Review: `layer(base, over)`
+
+Each item of `docs/REVIEW-CHECKLIST.md`, with the file and line that satisfies it.
+
+1. **Met.** `src/layer.mjs:49` exports `layer`.
+2. **Met.** `src/layer.mjs:25-37` (`lay`): a key of `base` that `over` lacks is
+   kept (line 29), two plain objects under one key are layered by recursion
+   (line 30), anything else in `over` replaces (line 31), and a key only `over`
+   has is kept (line 34). Tests: the checklist example at
+   `tests/layer.test.mjs:19`; any depth at `:30`; an array, replaced whole, at
+   `:38`; a number at `:45`; a string at `:51`; a boolean at `:57`; `null` at
+   `:63`. Each of those five replaces a number or string, a plain object and
+   an array in `base`.
+3. **Met.** `src/layer.mjs:50-51` throw a `TypeError` unless `isPlainObject`
+   (`src/layer.mjs:3-7`) holds for both arguments. Tests, each for both
+   arguments: an array at `tests/layer.test.mjs:75`, `null` at `:80`, a string
+   at `:85`, a number at `:90`, a `Date` at `:95`, an argument left out at
+   `:100`.
+4. **Met.** Every value that enters the result goes through `copy`
+   (`src/layer.mjs:13-23`) or is a fresh object made by `lay`
+   (`src/layer.mjs:26`); neither writes to its input. Tests: both layers
+   frozen all the way down and compared afterwards at
+   `tests/layer.test.mjs:106`; no object or array of the result is one of
+   either layer, at any depth and inside arrays, and changing the result
+   leaves both layers as they were, at `:117`.
+5. **Met.** `src/layer.mjs:20`, `:28` and `:34` skip the three key names in
+   `copy` (which also handles objects inside arrays, line 16) and in `lay`;
+   every object of the result is made by `{}` (`src/layer.mjs:18`, `:26`).
+   Tests: `tests/layer.test.mjs:149` (both arguments, nested, inside arrays,
+   and `Object.prototype` left clean) and `:167` (layers without a prototype
+   still give ordinary objects).
+6. **Met.** `CHANGELOG.md:5`.
+7. **Met.** `npm test`: 23 tests, 23 pass, 0 skipped, 0 todo, exit 0.
+8. **Met.** Changed in this project: `src/layer.mjs`, `tests/layer.test.mjs`,
+   `CHANGELOG.md`, and this file. `README.md` does not mention `layer`,
+   because this item rules that change out.
+
+## Decisions the task and checklist leave open
+
+- An object with no prototype (`Object.create(null)`, as `util.parseArgs`
+  returns) counts as a plain object; in the result it is an ordinary object.
+- A `Date` inside a layer (TOML has dates) is copied, so item 4 holds for it.
+- Any other object that is not plain data (a `Map`, a class instance, a
+  function) inside a layer throws a `TypeError` (`src/layer.mjs:17`, test at
+  `tests/layer.test.mjs:177`): it could not be put in the result without
+  sharing it.
+- A key that `over` holds with the value `undefined` replaces the value in
+  `base`, like any other value given in `over`.
+- Only enumerable string keys are read; symbol keys are not carried over.
+- A layer that contains itself is not detected and overflows the stack.
